.SH DESCRIPTION
Deserializes a JSON string into a bash \f[CR]COMMAND\f[R] tree.
Reconstructs the full AST from JSON produced by
\f[CR]cmd_serialize()\f[R], allocating all necessary structures
(\f[CR]COMMAND\f[R], \f[CR]SIMPLE_COM\f[R], \f[CR]CONNECTION\f[R],
\f[CR]FOR_COM\f[R], \f[CR]IF_COM\f[R], \f[CR]WHILE_COM\f[R],
\f[CR]CASE_COM\f[R], \f[CR]GROUP_COM\f[R], \f[CR]SUBSHELL_COM\f[R],
\f[CR]FUNCTION_DEF\f[R], \f[CR]WORD_LIST\f[R], \f[CR]WORD_DESC\f[R],
\f[CR]REDIRECT\f[R], \f[CR]PATTERN_LIST\f[R]).
.PP
The resulting COMMAND tree is compatible with
\f[CR]execute_command()\f[R] for pre\-parsed command execution, or can
be inspected and modified by clients.
.PP
Uses a simplified JSON parser internally (\f[CR]json_find_key()\f[R],
\f[CR]json_skip_value()\f[R], \f[CR]json_extract_string()\f[R],
\f[CR]json_extract_int()\f[R]) that handles nested objects, arrays,
strings, numbers, booleans, and null values.
